cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use material from this repository, please cite Samuil Petkov using
  the metadata below and follow the CC BY 4.0 attribution requirements.
  The version and release date are retained from the earlier Problem 625 package;
  the current Problem 625 manuscript is in 625/arxiv.
title: "Erdős Problem 625: Manuscript and Lean Formalization"
authors:
  - family-names: Petkov
    given-names: Samuil
date-released: 2026-08-27
version: 1.0.0
url: "https://github.com/SamPetkov/Erdos"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SamPetkov/Erdos"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A manuscript presenting a proposed positive resolution of Erdős Problem 625,
  accompanied by a Lean 4 formalization of the explicit full-sequence
  fixed-coefficient consequence. The phase-resolved refinement, quantified
  remainder, and failure-probability bound are proved in the manuscript.
  The manuscript is a preprint and has not undergone external peer review.
keywords:
  - Erdős problems
  - random graphs
  - chromatic number
  - cochromatic number
  - Lean 4
  - formalization
